       operator - C operator precedence and order of evaluation

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This manual page lists C operators and their precedence in evaluation.

       lb lb lb l l l.  Operator  Associativity  Notes () _Generic()  ‐    [1]
       []  ()  .  ->  ++  -- (type){} left to right  [2] [3] ++ -- & * + - ~ !
       _Countof sizeof alignof     right to left  [4] (type)    right to  left
       *  / %     left to right + -  left to right << >>     left to right < >
       <= >= left  to  right  ==  !=     left  to  right  &    left  to  right
       ^    left  to  right |    left to right &&   left to right ||   left to
       right ?:   right to left = *= /= %= += -= <<= >>= &=  ^=  |=  right  to
       left ,    left to right

       The following notes provide further information to the above table:

       [1]  The () at this precedence is the parenthesized expression.
       [2]  The () at this precedence is the function call operator.
       [3]  The  ++  and -- operators at this precedence level are the postfix
            flavors of the operators.
       [4]  The ++ and -- operators at this precedence level  are  the  prefix
            flavors of the operators.

